<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Functional Requirements Document (FRD) – &lt;System name&gt;</title>
<style>body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.45}h1{font-size:22pt;color:#2E3192}h2{font-size:14pt;color:#2E3192;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc}table{border-collapse:collapse}td{border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 10px}</style></head>
<body><h1>Functional Requirements Document (FRD) – &lt;System name&gt;</h1><p>Every requirement numbered, testable and traced to a business requirement.</p><table><tr><td>Document owner</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Version / status</td><td>v0.1 · Draft</td></tr><tr><td>Reviewers / approvers</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Last updated</td><td></td></tr></table>
<h2>1. Introduction</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Purpose, scope, references to the approved BRD, glossary.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>2. System overview</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Context diagram, users and roles, systems involved.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>3. Use cases / user stories</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Actor, preconditions, main flow, alternate flows, exceptions, postconditions.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>4. Functional requirements</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>FR-IDs: &#x27;The system shall…&#x27;, priority, linked BR-ID, acceptance criteria (Given / When / Then).</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>5. Business rules</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Calculations, validations, eligibility rules, decision tables.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>6. Data requirements</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Data dictionary: field, type, length, mandatory, source, validation; entity diagram.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>7. Interfaces and integrations</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>APIs, file formats, third-party systems, frequency, error handling.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>8. UI requirements</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Screens, wireframes, field behaviour, messages.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>9. Reports and dashboards</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Report name, users, filters, metrics, refresh frequency.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>10. Non-functional requirements</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Performance, availability, security, audit, accessibility, data retention.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>11. Traceability matrix (RTM)</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>BR-ID → FR-ID → test case ID, so nothing is missed.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2>12. Assumptions, open issues and sign-off</h2><p style='color:#666'><i>Open items with owners; sign-off by business and tech.</i></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p style="color:#888;font-size:9pt">Template from SkillNavora · skillnavora.in · Write it faster with the free AI writer: skillnavora.in/prd-writer</p></body></html>